      "description": "Watch Union St. Gilloise vs Bodo/Glimt highlights and goals from UEFA Champions League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 4, 2026. The UEFA Champions League stage was set for a high-octane encounter as Union St. Gilloise faced off against Bodo/Glimt in a contest filled with attacking intent. Both sides looked to assert their dominance early in a game that would keep fans on the edge of their seats until the final whistle. A High-Octane Opening Half The match on August 4, 2026 , exploded into life early on, with both teams showing no signs of hesitation. Bodo/Glimt drew first blood in the 20th minute when Patrick Berg found the back of the net. The lead, however, was short-lived as Raul Florucz equalized for the hosts just five minutes later. The back-and-forth nature of the game continued when Ole Blomberg clinicaly converted a penalty in the 29th minute to restore the Norwegian side's advantage. As the first half drew to a close, Union St. Gilloise found a crucial breakthrough in stoppage time. In the 45+5th minute, Guilherme Smith provided a brilliant assist for Raul Florucz , who netted his second goal of the night to level the score at 2-2. The first period was as feisty as it was high-scoring, with Massire Sylla , Kevin Mac Allister , and Anan Khalaili all receiving yellow cards as the physical battle intensified. Tactical Shifts and Sustained Pressure The second half saw both managers turn to their benches to break the deadlock. Bodo/Glimt introduced Andreas Helmersen and Joshua Kitolano at the restart, while the hosts made a triple substitution in the 56th minute, bringing on Kevin Rodriguez , Nikki Havenaar , and Besfort Zeneli . The middle period of the match became a tactical chess match, with yellow cards for Jostein Gundersen and Sondre Brunstad Fet reflecting the high stakes of the competition. Late Drama and a Last-Gasp Equalizer Just as it seemed the points would be shared, the match reached a dramatic crescendo in the final minutes. In the 88th minute, substitute Promise David latched onto a pass from Kevin Rodriguez to fire Union St. Gilloise into a 3-2 lead. The home fans were dreaming of a famous victory, but the drama was far from over. In the 91st minute, Patrick Berg turned provider, setting up Odin Luraas Bjoertuft for a stunning equalizer that silenced the home crowd. The referee blew the final whistle at 90+6 minutes, ending a classic UEFA Champions League encounter that finished 3-3, leaving both teams with a point after an unforgettable night of football."
